        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T05:29:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most of the discussion is captured in the attached bug and the linked doc, as well as b/154845324\nToshak suggested a 2W margin since barreljacks can provide an oversupply of current for a short period.\nI imagine we may tune these. Potentially we can treat the barreljack with no margin and force a 2W margin on the type-C i.e force throttling when power gets to type-C supply - 2W so that we have some leeway and not exceed the Type C supply.",
      "parentUuid": "55bd1dc0_092f0685",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 702,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 702,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "af4856daa1b9f58dd1d98e232e6a86e3b8574e55",
