        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T04:51:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This loses the old property that you could never overload this rail by connecting a device. Is that safe? (At a low duty cycle I\u0027d think so, but it\u0027s getting very close to the absolute maximum ratings for the regulator and its output inductor.)\n\nIn general this code seems to assume that it\u0027s safe to temporarily overload the power supply, but doesn\u0027t seem to explain that anywhere- could some explanation be added to the big comment block that explains the goals and operation?",
      "revId": "af4856daa1b9f58dd1d98e232e6a86e3b8574e55",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "05f75cde_e5dba5c5",
        "filename": "board/puff/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 750,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T05:46:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you mean that we are not allowing any headroom and if we are running on the edge then\nadding a new device may briefly exceed the rating?\nThe function is also run on-demand if any of the overcurrent interrupts occur, so the time it exceeds should be low, but agree if this is an issue, it would be much better to preserve some margin of error - I am not sure what that should be (it would be easy to just decrease the max power by whatever margin we deem appropriate).",
      "parentUuid": "1fa9c0f2_7f654027",
      "revId": "af4856daa1b9f58dd1d98e232e6a86e3b8574e55",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "423e3b28_a6bc2f84",
        "filename": "board/puff/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 750,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-05T02:37:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it\u0027s mostly a question of what kind of overload we can handle and for how long. In the worst case we can end up something like 1.8A over on the 5V rail (nearly 10W over in total power), which seems too high.",
      "parentUuid": "05f75cde_e5dba5c5",
      "revId": "af4856daa1b9f58dd1d98e232e6a86e3b8574e55",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e2291c3_a0bbc8fb",
        "filename": "board/puff/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 750,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-23T01:11:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consensus seems to be that short ~10ms overloads are probably not an issue, though it would be nice to actually test that kind of load to ensure it\u0027s okay.",
      "parentUuid": "423e3b28_a6bc2f84",
      "revId": "af4856daa1b9f58dd1d98e232e6a86e3b8574e55",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
